{"skill":{"slug":"agent-memory","displayName":"Agent Memory"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1769896232617,"changelog":"Initial release - SQLite-backed persistent memory for AI agents","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"README.md","size":5617,"sha256":"4598c26fd23e2218417cb666d18dbcf971c805d5887dbd205eeb846a0f81dbde","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":1385,"sha256":"7de6c27f611b9abf3928eaeeda14b850fcc852831db9e0087516e5612bd5aa72","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"cli/entity.py","size":3626,"sha256":"34bf34dad6b73e48f20ab61e83e3dba1ab1beadcc7d05885f6dac66a9def17dc","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"cli/fact.py","size":3462,"sha256":"de3eab5852fe233a90955380a4620d077e9df5db9d0d97cdb07f37e84c4784e3","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"cli/learn.py","size":2392,"sha256":"827e5700253c754605975d367ab9f2d6d6c6806467fdd8eb72fd029fdff4584d","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"examples/basic_usage.py","size":2848,"sha256":"2d4aee57035cb5db1c0dfbfd609d2d2f55913ecee0e40d26fbbbc5ff48651ab2","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"requirements.txt","size":48,"sha256":"8c0ba1c2073a16ba91088673bcdd919b49778f3c99636e26132876d6c21a6da3","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"src/__init__.py","size":212,"sha256":"1e54d9d2881854ff3b1c77775b68b8539aa653ba9cf83f275aa9ac9b8b50243d","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"src/memory.py","size":22097,"sha256":"296dec24ca81fc42f118b7dd5a09c27918968a89bed94ec718c7c1881a109cb3","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"tests/test_memory.py","size":5253,"sha256":"4a726aa0db0ee8a53b37a9c80332ac8f8dc77eb4cd713352314e1a4536f64822","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2391,"sha256":"1dad07813b5bbf8759e6ef8a043f7f2156b6a6d5352f24b2b4d92706face8529","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789025480800,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"1c63802f41b8e6523f6779cbbd5f1fece5f9c4f357eec7c3de1c705d94e09ef4","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/1c63802f41b8e6523f6779cbbd5f1fece5f9c4f357eec7c3de1c705d94e09ef4","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: agent-memory\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\nThe OpenClaw AgentMemory skill bundle is a self-contained, SQLite-based persistent memory system for AI agents. All code and documentation are aligned with its stated purpose of storing facts, lessons, and entities. There is no evidence of data exfiltration, malicious execution, persistence mechanisms, obfuscation, or prompt injection attempts against the analyzing agent. The skill uses standard Python libraries, manages its database in a user-specific directory (`~/.agent-memory/memory.db`), and explicitly states 'No external dependencies' in `requirements.txt`, indicating a low supply chain risk.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779160541859},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":16,"severity":"LOW","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":7,"checkedAt":1789025480800},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill is a local persistent memory library for agents, and its main risks are expected for that purpose but should be handled carefully.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The default database is created under ~/.agent-memory/memory.db, with optional custom or in-memory storage. Local disk persistence is proportionate to the skill's purpose, but stored memories are plaintext.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"Installation is presented as a ClawdHub install, git clone, or copying the Python file. requirements.txt declares no external dependencies, and the artifact does not contain install-time scripts or dependency-based payloads.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The SKILL.md suggests adding a session-start and session-end memory protocol to AGENTS.md or HEARTBEAT.md, including extracting durable facts from conversations. That is purpose-aligned, but users should review what gets saved.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The skill intentionally persists memory across sessions and provides permanent deletion and stale-cleanup operations. These are disclosed capabilities, but there is no built-in encryption, restrictive chmod enforcement, confirmation prompt, soft-delete, or undo.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The code and docs consistently implement agent memory: storing facts, lessons, entities, search, export, and cleanup in SQLite. I found no hidden networking, remote payload execution, tool hijacking, or unrelated system access.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Install only if you want an agent to keep local cross-session memory. Do not store secrets, credentials, regulated data, or sensitive personal information unless you have reviewed the storage path and local filesystem protections. Treat JSON exports and the SQLite database as private data, and use the forget/cleanup commands carefully because deletion is permanent.","findings":"[SQP-2] expected: The persistence and conversation-memory concerns are supported by the artifacts, but persistent local memory is the stated purpose and the database location is disclosed, so this is user guidance rather than a Review verdict by itself.\n[SQP-2] expected: Bulk export through export_json() is real and purpose-aligned. The artifact does not send exports anywhere, but users should treat exported memory as sensitive.\n[SQP-2] expected: The forget and forget_stale deletion paths are real and immediate. They can delete stored memories, but they are direct user/API operations for memory management rather than hidden destructive behavior.\n[T09] expected: The static scan's plaintext SQLite permission concern is valid as a hardening issue: default directory and database permissions rely on the process umask. It does not create remote access or exfiltration, and fits the local-memory purpose.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789025480800}}}}}